### 7. Test Book Reviews Endpoint
**cURL Command:**
```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/review/1
```

**Expected Output:**
```json
{}
```

**Note:** The reviews object is currently empty as no reviews have been added yet. This endpoint retrieves all reviews for the specified book by ISBN.

### 8. Test Add/Modify Book Review Endpoint (Authenticated)
**cURL Command:**
```bash
curl -X PUT "http://localhost:5000/customer/auth/review/1" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Cookie: session_cookie_here" -d "{\"review\":\"This is an excellent book about African culture and colonialism. Highly recommended!\"}"
```

**Expected Output:**
```json
{
    "message": "Review added/updated successfully"
}
```

**Note:** This endpoint requires user authentication (login session). The user must be logged in first. After adding a review, you can verify it was added by calling the book reviews endpoint again.

### 9. Test Delete Book Review Endpoint (Authenticated)
**cURL Command:**
```bash
curl -X DELETE "http://localhost:5000/customer/auth/review/1" -H "Cookie: session_cookie_here"
```

**Expected Output:**
```json
{
    "message": "Review deleted successfully"
}
```

**Note:** This endpoint allows authenticated users to delete only their own reviews. The user must be logged in and have an existing review for the specified book. Other users' reviews remain unaffected.

## Implementation Features
- ✅ User registration with validation
- ✅ User login with JWT authentication  
- ✅ Book listing with async-await pattern
- ✅ Book search by ISBN with Promise callbacks
- ✅ Book search by author with async operations
- ✅ Book search by title with error handling
- ✅ Book reviews endpoint
- ✅ Axios integration for HTTP requests
- ✅ Comprehensive error handling

## Repository Status
This repository demonstrates the complete implementation of an Express.js Book Reviews API as part of the IBM Developer Skills Network course. All endpoints have been successfully implemented with modern async-await patterns and proper error handling.